# =============================================================================
# CardDemo — Backend build-context exclusions (Docker).
#
# This file trims the `./backend` build context that `backend/Dockerfile`
# copies with `COPY --chown=appuser:appuser . .`. Everything matched here is
# NEVER sent to the Docker daemon and therefore can never land in an image
# layer. Two QA findings drive this file:
#
#   * F1 (image bloat): without exclusions, `COPY . .` baked the host virtual
#     environment (.venv/, ~162 MB and broken — its interpreter symlinks to the
#     host), byte-code/tool caches (__pycache__/, .ruff_cache/, .pytest_cache/),
#     and the full test suite (tests/) into the production image.
#   * F2 (latent secret-in-image): the documented dev workflow copies
#     `backend/.env.example` to `backend/.env`; excluding every `.env*` file
#     structurally guarantees a real secret file can never be copied into an
#     image layer (Ochs Rule #3 — secrets come from the runtime environment).
#
# Only production-runtime inputs (requirements.txt, app/, alembic/, alembic.ini,
# pyproject.toml) remain in the context.
# =============================================================================

# --- Python virtual environments (never used at runtime; broken host symlinks)
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
.python-version

# --- Byte-code and interpreter caches (regenerated; PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1)
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
*.pyd

# --- Test suite and test/tooling caches (not part of the runtime image)
tests/
# Dev/test dependency manifest (QA finding M-22): the runtime image installs
# only requirements.txt, so this file has no place in the build context.
requirements-dev.txt
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/

# --- Secret / environment files (F2: never bake a secret into the image).
#     `.env.example` is intentionally excluded too — the image needs no template.
.env
.env.*
*.env

# --- Packaging / build artifacts (rebuilt; not runtime inputs)
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# --- Version control and Docker meta (the image needs neither)
.git/
.gitignore
.dockerignore
Dockerfile

# --- OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- Logs and ad-hoc validation scratch files
*.log
blitzy_adhoc_test_*
